detailedAnswer:
Under the Hood:
Express 5 wraps handler execution in Promise resolution:
```javascript
const result = fn(req, res, next);
if (result && typeof result.then === 'function') {
  result.catch(next);
}
```
This eliminates monkey-patching packages like `express-async-errors` (which overwrote `Layer.prototype.handle_request`) and boilerplate wrapper functions like `const asyncHandler = fn => (req, res, next) => Promise.resolve(fn(req, res, next)).catch(next);`.

